# Pipeline Routing

## Step 0: Frontend Agent Selection

- Use `apps-senior-frontend` for mobile tasks (Expo, React Native, EAS, NativeWind mobile app flows).
- Use `web-senior-frontend` for web tasks (Next.js, App Router, React web).
- If the user explicitly names a frontend agent, use that agent with no override.

## Pipeline Matrix

- `full-stack`: analyst -> architect + designer -> frontend + backend -> qa
- `frontend-only`: analyst -> designer -> frontend -> qa
- `backend-only`: analyst -> architect -> backend -> qa
- `ui-fix`: frontend -> qa
- `api-fix`: backend -> qa
- `qa-only`: qa
- `analysis-only`: analyst

## Skip Rules

- Skip `designer` when no visual/UI changes are required.
- Skip `architect` when no new endpoint/service/schema decisions are required.
- Skip `backend` when no API or server-side behavior changes are required.
- Skip `analyst` when scope is bounded and implementation is straightforward.

## Parallel Rules

- `architect` and `designer` may run in parallel when both are needed.
- `frontend` and `backend` may run in parallel when their file domains do not overlap.
- Keep dependent steps sequential.
